<title>ESTONIA: NOON RADIO HEADLINES - MAY 13.</title>
<headline>NOON RADIO HEADLINES - MAY 13.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>These are the main headlines reported by Eesti Raadio on Tuesday at noon. Reuters has not verified these reports and cannot vouch for their accuracy.</p>
<p>-  The state budget has collected 3.64 billion kroons or 29.1 percent of its planned revenue for 1997 in the first four months of the year.</p>
<p>- Germany and Sweden support the Baltic countries' bids to join the European Union, German foreign minister Klaus Kinkel said.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
